  message: "DONE in PR #1870 (merged, dev cd60932590), with WI-donod. FOLD as the 2026-08-12 audit's DEPRECATE verdict proposed: `status` now means one thing, a shipped catalogue's completeness claim, and an overlay omits it; origin is ADR-0061's `provenance:`. The legacy `status: overlay` is still accepted (_LEGACY_OVERLAY_STATUS), as the 10-25 re-check required for shipped/seeded copies. The refusal that matters is preserved: provenance_declared is refused with the laundering reason; any other value is refused with its own reason (every value used to get the provenance_declared text). The 8 shipped community overlays, hypergumbo-self.yaml, the bash template, the catalogues-doc and repo-tier-offer samples drop the line; docs/CATALOGUES.md regenerated; ADR-0016 states the rule in place (the stale 'complete' wording went with it). LIVE REPRO ON MERGED DEV, production CLI `hypergumbo io-boundaries . --io-primitives F`: a file with NO status loads (rc 0, its mylib.ship row classifies: net_send 1); `status: overlay` loads (rc 0); `status: in_progress` rc 2 'declares status: 'in_progress'. `status` is a shipped catalogue's completeness claim and an overlay makes none, so omit the key...'; `status: provenance_declared` rc 2 '...a claim about a language's stdlib citation and is not available to an overlay. Omit `status`.' Tests: test_io_primitives_overlay.py::test_an_overlay_omits_status, ::test_status_overlay_is_still_accepted, ::test_an_overlay_may_not_claim_a_shipped_status, ::test_any_other_status_is_refused_with_its_own_reason[in_progress|complete|partial]."  # a03b
